{"version":"bsb","book":"psalms","chapter":15,"blocks":[{"kind":"heading","level":2,"text":"Who May Dwell on Your Holy Mountain?"},{"kind":"title","text":"A Psalm of David."},{"kind":"break"},{"kind":"poetry","indent":1,"runs":[{"verse":1,"end":null,"start":true,"text":"O LORD, who may abide in Your tent?"}]},{"kind":"poetry","indent":2,"runs":[{"verse":1,"end":null,"start":false,"text":"Who may dwell on Your holy mountain?"}]},{"kind":"break"},{"kind":"poetry","indent":1,"runs":[{"verse":2,"end":null,"start":true,"text":"He who walks with integrity"}]},{"kind":"poetry","indent":2,"runs":[{"verse":2,"end":null,"start":false,"text":"and practices righteousness,"}]},{"kind":"poetry","indent":2,"runs":[{"verse":2,"end":null,"start":false,"text":"who speaks the truth from his heart,"}]},{"kind":"poetry","indent":1,"runs":[{"verse":3,"end":null,"start":true,"text":"who has no slander on his tongue,"}]},{"kind":"poetry","indent":2,"runs":[{"verse":3,"end":null,"start":false,"text":"who does no harm to his neighbor,"}]},{"kind":"poetry","indent":2,"runs":[{"verse":3,"end":null,"start":false,"text":"who casts no scorn on his friend,"}]},{"kind":"poetry","indent":1,"runs":[{"verse":4,"end":null,"start":true,"text":"who despises the vile"}]},{"kind":"poetry","indent":2,"runs":[{"verse":4,"end":null,"start":false,"text":"but honors those who fear the LORD,"}]},{"kind":"poetry","indent":2,"runs":[{"verse":4,"end":null,"start":false,"text":"who does not revise a costly oath,"}]},{"kind":"poetry","indent":1,"runs":[{"verse":5,"end":null,"start":true,"text":"who lends his money without interest"}]},{"kind":"poetry","indent":2,"runs":[{"verse":5,"end":null,"start":false,"text":"and refuses a bribe against the innocent."}]},{"kind":"break"},{"kind":"poetry","indent":1,"runs":[{"verse":5,"end":null,"start":false,"text":"He who does these things"}]},{"kind":"poetry","indent":2,"runs":[{"verse":5,"end":null,"start":false,"text":"will never be shaken."}]}]}
